{
  "id": "Compound::DB00988 - Gene::6530",
  "verbalization": "Dopamine is linked to Slc6a2 through a series of molecular interactions that involve transport and signaling mechanisms. The evidence suggests that Dopamine, as a catecholamine, binds to Slc22a1 and Slc22a3, which are both involved in the transport of monoamines across cellular membranes. These transporters are part of a broader functional pathway that ultimately leads to the participation of Slc6a2 in monoamine transmembrane transport. This implies that Dopamine may influence Slc6a2 through its role in modulating the activity of these transporters, thereby affecting the transport of norepinephrine and other monoamines across cell membranes. The shared involvement of Slc6a2 in these processes, as well as the hierarchical relationships between dopamine, catecholamines, and transporters, supports a mechanism where Dopamine exerts a regulatory effect on Slc6a2 through its interaction with these transporters.",
